  <section class="product-section" aria-labelledby="protection-heading">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Protection</p>
      <h2 id="protection-heading">Three simple layers.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="protection-grid">
      <article class="protection-card">
        <span class="protection-index">01</span>
        <h3>Reverse polarity</h3>
        <p>A P-channel MOSFET blocks power when the source is connected backward without adding a series diode to the normal current path.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="protection-card">
        <span class="protection-index">02</span>
        <h3>Transient clamp</h3>
        <p>A TVS diode clamps short voltage spikes before they reach the protected circuit.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="protection-card">
        <span class="protection-index">03</span>
        <h3>Resettable fuse</h3>
        <p>A polyfuse limits sustained fault current and resets after the fault is removed and the device cools.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

